# Session handoffs — deliberately NOT published.
#
# These are working notes for continuing the project, not documentation anyone else can use,
# and they carry the owner's email and the hub's LAN address. They live here rather than
# outside the repo so every doc pointer and every session's habits keep working; they are
# simply never committed. Purged from history 2026-08-20, before the first push.
#
# ⚠️ They are the project's memory. Back them up separately — git is not doing it.
docs/handoff/

# Agent/owner working layer — deliberately NOT published, purged from history 2026-08-20.
#
# `CLAUDE.md` is Claude Code's project-instructions file and `intro.md` is the orientation
# document it points at. Both describe *this machine* — the Home Assistant add-on container,
# the venv at /homeassistant/scripts/kohler-work, which restart does what — and would mislead
# anyone who cloned the repo, since none of those paths exist for them. They also name the
# owner. Nothing published links to either; the protocol content they summarise lives in
# docs/ where it belongs.
#
# ⚠️ Like docs/handoff/, git is not backing these up.
CLAUDE.md
intro.md
